      ],
      "reason": "Scope-owned runtime WeakMap exposes same-connection typed initialize.codexHome/userAgent plus v2 thread/loaded/list evidence. No provider-name/version cache, second process or prompt probe. Legacy adoption reads actual schema-native thread ID/cwd/idle state and completed turn refs (paginated history supported) before resume. Native completed-turn historical fork continues through original inclusive lastTurnId API; sidecar remains current Chat records."
    },
    {
      "id": "PM-CODEX-OWNED-MCP-AND-CONTEXT",
      "paths": [
        "apps/server/src/orchestration-v2/Adapters/CodexAdapterV2.ts",
        "apps/server/src/provider/CodexDeveloperInstructions.ts"
      ],
      "reason": "Original ensure/resume/fork receive only generation-bound RuntimeHost stdio MCP entries. The original openSession host binding's threadId/executionId are captured once and included at both native background-command and child-subagent continuation offer sites, never replaced with a later binding; the continuation factory receives the same runtimeHost. Turn context contains generic native harness identity, never t3 orchestration/browser/device/PR tooling. PM permission/approval/revision/receipt authority remains unchanged; original native tool/output/subagent streams remain display/interaction events only."
    },
    {
      "id": "PM-CODEX-HOME-AND-INSTALLER-CONTINUITY",
